  "notes": "Keyword lists for the safety module. Ventriloquist never proposes a message, word or completion that matches any entry, and flags a spelled message that matches one for in-person verification by a caregiver. Lists favour recall over precision: a false positive only shows the verification banner. Entries are uppercase A-Z; multi-word phrases are listed both with single spaces and with the spaces removed, because patients spell without punctuation or word breaks. Matching guidance: (1) normalise the spelled text to A-Z and spaces, then test each entry against both the spaced text and a copy with all spaces removed; (2) check both languages' lists whatever the session language, since bilingual patients mix them; (3) short entries such as DIE, DEAD, KILL, MATI, MAUT, SIGN, BANK, ATM, IZIN and DNR also occur inside harmless words (DIET, LADIES, SKILL, MATIKAN, AMATI, DESIGN, PERIZINAN); match them as whole words when word boundaries are known and accept the substring false positives when they are not. Categories overlap on purpose (for example LET ME DIE, MATI, WASIAT, TANDA TANGAN, POWER OF ATTORNEY); report every category that matches. These lists are a starting point written by the project team, not a validated clinical instrument, and must be reviewed by ICU clinicians and Indonesian speakers before any real use."
}
